# Identity keys, and nothing else that is secret.
#
# This project tracked build/ and run/ on purpose for a long time, and this file is not a
# reversal of that so much as the end of it. These are the two exceptions that decision
# never considered: unencrypted private keys, and 80 MB of somebody's dev worlds in a
# public repository.
#
# Three keys were published from `b1f35e7` until 2026-08-24 — the dedicated server's and
# the Alice and Bob dev identities. The server key was rotated, because it had signed
# nothing that survives. The other two were not, deliberately: they unlock nothing but
# make-believe markets on one machine, and rotating them would make this machine a
# stranger to its own test worlds. A key in git history cannot be recalled; rotating is
# what makes a published one worthless, and this file is what stops the next one.
*.key

# Build output and dev worlds.
#
# Tracked until 2026-08-25, which is why a clone of this repository is 328 MB of somebody
# else's saved games and compiled classes. The history keeps them and only a rewrite would
# not — but nothing new lands here, and a browser now sees src, docs and a README rather
# than run/saves/asdhaskjdha.
build/
run/
.gradle/
